%!PS
% Test content for poem.ps: the content of the poem brief that the blind
% reviews of issue #108 judged (Basho's old pond, three notes, ASCII text
% with straight apostrophes); paper theme. The English is a word-for-word
% rendering written for that brief.
% `psanim check poem-basho.ps` runs poem.ps with this content.
/tpl (poem.ps) component
/film /tpl << /Params <<
  /look /paper
  /heading (Basho's old pond)
  /poet (Matsuo Basho, 1686; literal rendering)
  /poem [ (old pond) (a frog jumps in) (the sound of water) ]
  /notes [
    [ 0 (old pond) (image)
      (The scene is set in two words: something old, still and silent, before anything happens.) ]
    [ 1 (a frog jumps in) (turn)
      (The only movement in the poem, and it is over in an instant.) ]
    [ 2 (the sound of water) (sound)
      (The poem ends on a sound, and on the silence that comes back after it.) ]
  ]
  /reading (A brief sound makes the stillness around it noticeable. The pond is quiet before and after; the frog is only a moment.)
>> >> instance
<< /Size [1280 720] /Duration /film componentduration /FPS 30 >> animation
/scene { /film << /After /hold >> place } def
